  "needs": [
    "ARRANGEMENT per ref/mounting.md (manual + photo research): two reflectors fore/aft of the cabin, axes in ONE common vertical plane (manual l.1584-1585). LOWER/FRONT reflector near-VERTICAL (~15°), low, in front of the box, concave up-&-rearward toward the throat. UPPER/REAR reflector strongly LAID BACK (~45°), high, behind the box, concave up-&-forward toward the throat. The asymmetric tilt (upright front / laid-back rear) is the signature P-37 silhouette.",
    "SUPPORT = a triangulated tubular cradle (NOT single arms): each reflector held by an UPPER arm + a LOWER boom (a triangle to its backing) mirrored at x≈±0.8, plus rear stay tie-rods from the tower base down to the trailer corners (photos w24/w20/w17/w12/w05). Modelled with the `pipe` operator. Coordinates from ref/mounting.md (photo-estimated).",
    "Reflectors IDENTICAL: 9.7 × 3.0 m, focal 2.5 m, asymmetric offset-fed paraboloid cut (manual l.194-196). Width-curve approx (curve 0.55); top-clipped pentagon.",
    "Feeds: each reflector has its own feed column at its 2.5 m focus in the central throat (manual l.1983-1987). LOWER = 3 flared horns; UPPER = 2 horns + an 8-dipole line bar (l.1843-1854). Curved waveguides (`pipe`) cabin→feed.",
    "Central tower: tapered tubular X-braced lattice (`tubeMast`) rising from the cabin roof and LEANING REARWARD (apexZ −0.7), base→apex per mounting.md. Tilt angles, fore/aft offset (~4.3 m), vertical gap (~2 m) and tower height are PHOTO-ESTIMATED (no metric source); operational focal-axis angles +3.5°/+10.5° are sourced but are not the museum display pose we match.",
    "Trailer 52-У-415М: SINGLE fat road wheel per station, 2 axles, tyre + hub drum + 8 lug bolts + rounded hub-cap dome (`wheel`). Underframe X-bracing (`pipe`). Cabin 636А, turntable, drawbar+tow eye, nose jack, 4 outrigger jacks, fenders, az-motor OBSERVED from the walkaround.",
    "Cabin ladder + richer feed-horn detail remain TODO. Total deployed height & system weight UNSOURCED. Livery photo-observed.",
    "External 3D ref (Sketchfab Militman 'Draft | Radar P37') is low-poly/undocumented — NOT authoritative; manual + walkaround photos used instead."
  ]
